  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CDC-Promote implementing of Democary Law</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quang Binh Community Development Center (CDC) has initiated a project with the aim of promoting effective practice of the Law on Implementation of Grassroots-level Democracy in the rural area, specifically 3 rural, coastal and mountainous areas in Le Thuy district, Quang Binh province. The project&#x2019;s prior objective is to raise awareness of rights and obligations of the people and local authorities on disseminating the Law on Implementation of Grassroots-level Democracy through diverse activities of the core group. Importantly, the Organize corresponding training courses to build capacity for people and local authorities so that the parties can well implement the contents specified in the Law on Implementation of Grassroots Democracy. Besides, CDC also expects to be able to create opportunities for the citizens and local authorities to have shared space in order to promote transparency and openness in the locality. Furthermore, the initiative also targets to share experiences and disseminate information in the projected communes to gradually replicate the model throughout Quang Binh province. The expect outcomes of this initiative are: raising legal awareness and approach based on democratic rights at grassroots level for at least 1200 people (women account for at least 45%); 6 sharing seminars between people and the local authority with at least 420 participants (in which 40% are women); at least 1 proposal will be send to governmental agencies about people&#x2019;s confusion during the implementation of the Law on Implementation of Grassroots-level Democracy.</narrative>
  </description>
