   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&apos;CDC has over 10 years of experience in promoting community development in both rural and urban areas in order to help people improve their quality of life through capacity building and supporting them in their. We put an emphasis on: i) community development; ii) Promote grassroots democracy; Child Rights, Gender and Development; iii) Agriculture and Rural Development. CDC has carried out many projects to promote human rights, including activities to disseminate laws on the Ordinance on exercising democracy, Child RightsConvention, the Laws on Gender Equality and Prevention of Trafficking, and support the implementation of community initiatives on the basis of &quot;people know, people discuss, people do#, people monitor&quot;, children self-governing groups, economic empowerment for women,# in Quang Binh province. Since its foundation, the CDC has worked in according with laws and regulations in Vietnam.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quang Binh Community Development Ce</narrative>
